WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.425
This is Allen Company training on abandoned areas

00:07.425 --> 00:10.525
underground, and on barricading as a last resort

00:10.525 --> 00:13.513
in an emergency. Abandoned or worked-out areas

00:13.513 --> 00:17.425
can hold bad air, low oxygen, loose roof and ribs,

00:17.425 --> 00:20.712
and water. They aren't examined like active areas.

00:21.828 --> 00:24.503
Hazardous areas are barricaded, or posted with

00:24.503 --> 00:27.466
warning signs at every approach that can be seen.

00:27.466 --> 00:30.266
Never go past a barricade or a danger sign unless

00:30.266 --> 00:32.191
you've been assigned and trained to,

00:32.191 --> 00:34.041
and the area has been examined.

00:35.166 --> 00:37.641
Your mine map shows where the abandoned and sealed

00:37.641 --> 00:41.066
areas are. Learn them, and how they're marked underground,

00:41.066 --> 00:42.241
on your mine tour.

00:45.568 --> 00:49.118
In a fire, your first job is always to escape,

00:49.118 --> 00:51.793
by your primary escapeway or your secondary if

00:51.793 --> 00:54.968
the first is blocked. Barricading is only for when

00:54.968 --> 00:56.793
every way out is cut off.

00:57.934 --> 01:00.647
If miners can't reach the surface through two separate

01:00.647 --> 01:03.385
escapeways within an hour, the mine must provide

01:03.385 --> 01:06.297
a method of refuge. None of Allen's mines has a

01:06.297 --> 01:07.885
designated refuge.

01:09.004 --> 01:11.679
If you must barricade: pick a spot with the best

01:11.679 --> 01:14.804
air you can find, as much space as possible,

01:14.804 --> 01:17.704
away from the smoke. Build the barricade with posts

01:17.704 --> 01:20.391
and brattice cloth, and seal the edges with fine

01:20.391 --> 01:23.629
rock or dust. Leave a sign outside saying who is

01:23.629 --> 01:26.604
inside and when you went in. Build a second curtain

01:26.604 --> 01:28.317
for an air lock if you can.

01:29.446 --> 01:32.971
Inside, stay calm, stay still to save air,

01:32.971 --> 01:35.609
use one light at a time, keep your self-rescuer

01:35.609 --> 01:38.796
ready, and signal by tapping on pipes or roof bolts

01:38.796 --> 01:39.821
at intervals.

01:40.936 --> 01:43.948
Recap: stay out of abandoned areas and never cross

01:43.948 --> 01:46.961
a barricade or danger sign. Escape first,

01:46.961 --> 01:50.686
by either escapeway. Barricade only as a last resort,

01:50.686 --> 01:52.599
mark it, and conserve air.

01:53.722 --> 01:56.885
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

01:56.885 --> 01:58.385
override this video.
